  "comments": "Mint mark: Head of Archangel Michael, Koninklijke Munt van België - Monnaie Royal de Belgique, Brussels, Belgium<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">Three main groups of Obverse are known</span><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Obverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">I</span> - earlobe with curved outline.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">II</span> - earlobe with angled outline in fine line.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">III</span> - smaller earlobe with angled outline in thick line.<br /><br />\r\nTogether with these features there are many more, some of which are marked by arrows.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5f78cbeb80e25.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5f78cbeb80e25.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"198\" /></a>",
